.SH "Member Function Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "template<uint32_t dim> void \fBcsmp::MohrCoulombFailure_Visitor\fP< dim >::Visit (\fBElement\fP< dim > * e)\fR [virtual]\fP"
Loops over the element integration points and evaluates shear and tensile failure potential\&. Where failure occurred the variable 'failure' is set to 1\&. A distinction is made between tensile 'tensile failure' and shear failure 'failure' variables\&.

.PP
\fBAttention\fP
.RS 4
it is assumed that the tensile strength is about 1/10 of the cohesive strength of the rock

.PP
SKM 28/9/2014 - added case where stress is placed on the element\&. 
.RE
.PP

